✅ async/await kya hota hai?
async/await JavaScript mein Promises ko handle karne ka modern aur easy way hai. Yeh asynchronous code ko likhne mein synchronous jaise feel deta hai — code readable aur clean ban jata hai.

🔹 Syntax:
javascript

async function myFunction() {
  let result = await someAsyncTask();
  console.log(result);
}
async function hamesha ek Promise return karta hai.

await kisi Promise ke result ka wait karta hai — bina next line pe jaaye.

🔹 Basic Example:
javascript

function waitOneSecond() {
  return new Promise(resolve => {
    setTimeout(() => {
      resolve("1 second ho gaya");
    }, 1000);
  });
}

async function run() {
  console.log("Start");
  const msg = await waitOneSecond();
  console.log(msg);
  console.log("End");
}

run();
🟢 Output:

sql

Start  
1 second ho gaya  
End
✅ Error Handling with try...catch:
javascript

async function fetchData() {
  try {
    const res = await fetch("https://api.example.com/data");
    const data = await res.json();
    console.log(data);
  } catch (err) {
    console.error("Error aaya:", err.message);
  }
}
🔹 Use Cases:
API call (REST API / fetch)

File operations in Node.js

Database queries

Delayed operations (setTimeout with Promises)

🔁 Summary:
Keyword	Use for
async	Function ko promise-returning banana
await	Promise ke result ka wait karna
